From 72a9ffde6f38a81a26ad5a279e59170817701afc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:54:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Check the iPhone before signing in, and register it alone
 after

The sign-ins that Cartouche's measurements saw stop at the device step
had all got through Apple, more than half of them after the player had
typed a verification code: LocalDevVPN was off or not carrying the
iPhone's traffic, the iPhone was not on Wi-Fi, or it refused the
pairing file. Signing in again then costs the player another code, and
Apple one more sign-in, which it limits.

Sign In to Cartouche now makes minimuxer's readiness check, the one the
device step and every pipeline make, before anything goes to Apple: a
pairing file loaded, Wi-Fi, LocalDevVPN connected and carrying the
iPhone's traffic, and the iPhone answering through it. SideStore starts
minimuxer as it launches, which can still be under way when the action
starts: the check waits for it, 15 seconds at most. A sign-in that does
not pass it stops at a new stage, deviceCheck, with minimuxer's error.

A new action, Register Cartouche's iPhone, takes the device step alone,
as SideStore's settings do from their pending actions: with the session
and the team SideStore kept after a sign-in that stopped there, the same
readiness check, then Apple's developer services. No sign-in, and no
code. Shortcuts does not list it. Cartouche's outcome names it device,
at the stages account (no session or team kept, for Cartouche to sign
in again), deviceCheck, device and finish.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
